Hi Rafael,

here is some more info:
-The board is based on an Intel Atom N2600 (attached is the output of
lshw if that is any help)
-Linus' kernel (3.9.0-rc4) does not seem to boot without acpi=off either

-Without any debug, the board always hangs at the "isapnp" line in the
following stanza:
BIOS EDD facility v0.16 2004-Jun-25, 0 devices found
EDD information not available.
isapnp: No Plug & Play device found
ata1: SATA link down (SStatus 0 SControl 300)


-I am not able to tell anything from the output of
"acpi.debug_layer=0xFFFFFFFF acpi.debug_level=0xFFFFFFFF" as there are
way too much messages (it seems and it doesn't seem to end (I could
let it run overnight to see if it gets stuck)

Attached are the last screen of output of the following patterns (on
kernel 3.5.7.6):
acpi.debug_layer=0x0000FFFF acpi.debug_level=FF000000 (*_104238.txt)
acpi.debug_layer=0x0000FFFF acpi.debug_level=00FF0000 (*_105043.txt)
acpi.debug_layer=0x0000FF00 acpi.debug_level=FFFF0000 (no output after
"EDD information" line)
acpi.debug_layer=0x000000FF acpi.debug_level=FFFF0000 (*_105835.txt)

Lastly, *_153235.jpg is a picture of the last screen of output of
Linus' kernel ran with "acpi.debug_layer=0xFFFFFFFF
acpi.debug_level=0xFCFFFFFF" (which should exclude only mutex and
thread information if I am not mistaken).

I am not sure what would be the most useful information to give, so
please let me know what is needed.

Regards,
Olivier

